Suppose we have a SkyNet output h5 file in the following path:

/some/path/out.h5

Follow these steps to make a movie:

$ cd /some/path
$ /path/to/SkyNet/installation/examples/plot_temp_rho_edot.py out.h5
$ mkdir chart_frames
$ /path/to/SkyNet/installation/examples/movie out.h5
$ ffmpeg -y -c:v png -i "chart_frames/chart_%06d.png" -pix_fmt yuv420p -c:v libx264 -preset slow -crf 1 "out.mp4"
